+# Telephone event groups: printed identifiers, zero fields and one reading caution
+
+October 27, 2026. Original-record goal track 2; existing AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. This is an additive test of selected held carrier-record images, not a new authenticated carrier release or a completed call reconstruction.
+
+**The selected records can now be grouped by their printed CSC/GS identifiers, rather than by start time alone. Two records with zero duration share an identifier and have start-to-event label spans of 46 and 59 seconds. Another printed identifier occurs on both zero-duration and 159-duration records.** These facts concern the printout's fields. They do not establish a conversation, its caller, its recipient, or the operational meaning of zero.
+
+This pass also qualifies our own earlier precise transcription of the routed-event time. Its source image has not changed. The former **07:26:28** reading remains preserved; the crossed digit is now recorded as uncertain between **07:26:18** and **07:26:28**. This is a reading limitation, not two historical source versions or evidence of tampering.
+
+## Inputs and actual reading scope
+
+The held [public reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/13499791/T7-B13-Flight-11-Calls-Fdr-Response-From-DOJ-to-Doc-Req-14-Calls-From-AA-11-and-77-and-UA-175-and-93-ATT-Wireless-UA-And-GTE-Airphone-Call-Record) supplies hosted JPEG reproductions of released records. The earlier [carrier-enclosure study](../telephone-carrier-enclosures-2026-10-27/README.md) acquired 28 current images and documented its page gap. This pass reuses unchanged images, checks their pinned bytes and reads five selected event blocks on reader pages 15, 16, 20 and 21. It does not acquire a complete agency-native Request 14 delivery, authenticate the uploader/release chain, inspect every AA77 event anew or provide native switching data.
+
+`SOURCE-PINS.json` gives exact public image URLs, source relationship, original access UTC, byte sizes and SHA-256 values. `EVENT-OBSERVATIONS.json` gives reader/Bates/block/native-pixel rectangles and safe field transcriptions. Full CSC/GS values, inspection crops and OCR remain local; they are not published. The public group names G18 and G25 are our temporary labels for this comparison, not carrier-provided caller identities or globally unique call IDs.
